                <pb facs="0689" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg669"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Lord
                        Lyons.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State.</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 5, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your communication of the 30th ultimo, relative to the refusal of a
                    clearance to Messrs. Darrell &amp; Nash on merchandise shipped by them to
                    Nassau, and, in reply, to inform your lordship that I have transmitted a copy
                    thereof to the Secretary of the Treasury, who has been requested to investigate
                    the case, with a view to the adoption of such proceedings as the result may
                    warrant.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, my lord, your obedient
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD,</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord Lyons,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
